## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
Issue #28 addresses CxxTest assertion failures that could be reported as a
passing evaluation with a generic process error when a one-test summary used
the singular word test.

### Decisions Made
- Reconcile CxxTest output and runner exit status in one helper so a nonzero,
unparseable runner cannot overwrite the outcome to passed.
- Treat parsed assertion failures as test failures and clear the generic
process-exit message, while preserving the complete CxxTest assertion line
for Results.
- Preserve compile-error and normal expected-output mismatch classifications.

### Verification
Docker integration exercises invalid C++, a one-test CxxTest assertion
failure, and a valid program with mismatched expected output.
